export const meta = {
  name: 'verify-phase67-context-facts',
  description: 'Adversarially verify the load-bearing TEE-worker code/spec facts before they are baked into Phase 67 CONTEXT.md',
  phases: [{ title: 'Verify', detail: 'parallel refutation of each fact cluster against live code/spec' }],
}

const VERDICT_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  additionalProperties: false,
  properties: {
    cluster: { type: 'string' },
    claims: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        additionalProperties: false,
        properties: {
          claim: { type: 'string' },
          verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['confirmed', 'corrected', 'unverifiable'] },
          evidence: { type: 'string', description: 'file:line reference(s) + a short verbatim quote proving the verdict' },
          correction: { type: 'string', description: 'if corrected/unverifiable, the accurate statement; empty string if confirmed' },
        },
        required: ['claim', 'verdict', 'evidence', 'correction'],
      },
    },
    summary: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['cluster', 'claims', 'summary'],
}

const COMMON = `You are a skeptical verifier. Do NOT trust the claim text — open the actual file(s) and try to REFUTE each claim. Only return verdict "confirmed" when the live code/spec proves it true, with a file:line reference and a short verbatim quote. If the claim is wrong, return "corrected" with the accurate statement. Read-only: do not modify any files. Work in /Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box.`

const CLUSTERS = [
  {
    label: 'tee-route-contract',
    prompt: `${COMMON}

Verify these claims about the CURRENT TEE worker republish contract:
1. apps/tee-worker/src/routes/republish.ts increments the IPNS sequence by 1 (the "+ 1n") and signs a relay-supplied CID taken from the request body (entry.latestCid), i.e. it ORIGINATES a fresh record from scalars rather than parsing/verifying an incoming marshaled signedRecord.
2. The TEE worker does NOT parse or verify any incoming signedRecord signature (no IPNS CBOR record parse + Ed25519 verify anywhere in apps/tee-worker/src).
3. The EOL/record lifetime is a hardcoded ~48h constant in apps/tee-worker/src/services/ipns-signer.ts (TEE_RECORD_LIFETIME_MS), set at record creation; there is NO "extend the EOL of an existing record" path.
Quote exact lines.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'signing-input-source',
    prompt: `${COMMON}

Verify these claims about where the TEE's signing inputs come from:
1. The relay builds the TEE request body from ipns_republish_schedule rows (apps/api/src/republish/republish.service.ts getDueEntries / the teeEntries map), NOT from the canonical ipns_records row.
2. apps/api/src/republish/republish-schedule.entity.ts has FOUR columns that duplicate ipns_records state: encryptedIpnsKey (encrypted_ipns_key), keyEpoch (key_epoch), latestCid (latest_cid), sequenceNumber (sequence_number).
3. The canonical ipns_records row is only WRITTEN BACK on success via syncIpnsRecordSequence, and that write-back is a LessThanOrEqual forward-only UPDATE (NOT an equality compare-and-set on sequence).
Quote exact lines + the column decorators.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'enclave-bindings-absent',
    prompt: `${COMMON}

Verify these claims about MISSING enclave hardening in the current TEE worker:
1. There is NO name<->key binding assertion (no check that publicKeyFromIpnsName(ipnsName) == pubkey(decryptedKey) == record.pubkey) anywhere in apps/tee-worker/src before signing.
2. There is NO tombstone / revoked-CID check in the TEE worker path (the relay's getDueEntries selects on status/nextRepublishAt only and does not join ipns_records.tombstoned_at).
3. The epoch the TEE uses is RELAY-SUPPLIED: apps/tee-worker/src/routes/republish.ts trusts entry.currentEpoch/entry.previousEpoch from the request body; key-manager.ts decryptWithFallback tries currentEpoch then previousEpoch; reEncryptForEpoch re-wraps to the relay-chosen currentEpoch (not an enclave-internally-derived epoch).
Quote exact lines (or state the absence with the grep you ran).`,
  },
  {
    label: 'phase66-cas-location',
    prompt: `${COMMON}

Verify these claims about the Phase-66 publish CAS vs the TEE renewal path:
1. The fused atomic compare-and-set (WHERE ipns_name = :n AND sequence_number = :expected AND generation <= :incoming AND tombstoned_at IS NULL; 0 rows => 409/410) lives in apps/api/src/ipns/ipns.service.ts upsertIpnsRecord.
2. The TEE renewal path does NOT route its write through upsertIpnsRecord — it publishes to delegated routing and writes back via republish.service.ts syncIpnsRecordSequence (the weaker LessThanOrEqual UPDATE), so the renewal write is NOT yet guarded by the same equality CAS.
3. apps/api/src/ipns/entities/ipns-record.entity.ts already has tombstonedAt (tombstoned_at) and generation columns and is named ipns_records with NO public_key column (Phase 66 rename done).
Quote exact lines.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'spec-sections',
    prompt: `${COMMON}

Open .planning/design/2026-06-26-sharing-read-keychaining-design.md and verify the content of these sections (quote the relevant lines verbatim):
1. §6.4 describes the TEE as a "record-lease-renewer": relay sends the marshaled existing signedRecord, TEE parses + verifies the signature + re-emits the SAME CID + SAME sequence with only a later EOL; cannot originate or repoint a CID.
2. §6.7 lists THREE enclave bindings: (1) internal epoch derivation from the TEE's own clock (never relay scalars) with re-wrap targeting an enclave-enumerated epoch; (2) name<->key binding publicKeyFromIpnsName(ipnsName) == pubkey(decryptedKey) == record.pubkey; (3) migration durability — and confirm whether it offers BOTH "client re-enroll recovery path" AND "refuse to renew keys older than currentEpoch − 1" as the two options.
3. §6.3 says collapse the dual-source state so ipns_records is the sole signing-input source and the schedule is reduced to scheduling metadata.
4. §7.3 test 12 — quote it verbatim (the "Republisher stale-CID" test about no-increment + revoked CID never re-signed).
Report each with the line numbers you found.`,
  },
  {
    label: 'test-infra-reality',
    prompt: `${COMMON}

